# 🛡️ DevShield

> **AI-powered security-first browser-based development environment for modern development teams.**

## 🚀 Overview

DevShield is an innovative browser-based IDE that provides **real-time security auditing** while you code. Built for mid-sized product companies and AI startups, it combines collaborative development with intelligent security analysis using advanced Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) parsing and graph-based vulnerability detection.

### ✨ Key Features

- 🛡️ **Real-time Security Auditing:** AI-powered vulnerability detection with AST and graph analysis.
- 🌐 **Browser-based IDE:** No local setup required, works anywhere with Monaco Editor.
- 🤝 **Collaborative Coding:** Multi-user real-time editing powered by Socket.io.
- 📊 **Security Analytics:** Comprehensive vulnerability reporting and contextual patch suggestions.
- 🔧 **Multi-language Support:** 165+ programming languages supported via Tree-sitter.
- 🧠 **Graph-based Analysis:** Advanced Code Property Graph (CPG) for deep data flow analysis.
- 🤖 **LLM Integration:** Groq API and local Ollama support for intelligent explanations and code fixes.

---

## 💡 Why DevShield?

Standard AI tools (like GitHub Copilot) often generate fixes that break logic or miss critical vulnerabilities. DevShield solves this by grounding AI in **code structure + data flow**.

| AI Limitation        | DevShield Solution                                      | Technology Used           |
|----------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------|
| **Syntax Errors** | Validates patches against **AST** before suggesting     | Tree-sitter, Monaco       |
| **Location Errors** | Injects fixes at the exact logical node                 | Code Property Graph (CPG) |
| **Semantic Drift** | Ensures logic consistency via **CFG tracking** | Control Flow Graph        |
| **Misleading Fixes** | Verifies secure flow using **Taint Analysis** | Data Flow Graph           |
| **Partial Fixes** | Detects cross-file issues via repo-wide analysis        | GNN Embeddings            |
| **Human Intent Gap** | Learns from accepted/rejected fixes                     | Feedback Loop             |

---

## 🏗️ System Architecture

DevShield operates on a three-tier microservice architecture, separating the user interface, file management, and heavy security analysis.

### Visual Flow

```text
            ┌────────────────────────────┐
            │        Frontend (UI)       │
            │----------------------------│
            │ • Monaco Editor            │
            │ • File Explorer            │
            │ • Xterm.js (Logs/AI)       │
            │ • Tailwind UI              │
            └────────────┬───────────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
            ┌────────────────────────────┐
            │    Backend (Node.js)       │
            │----------------------------│
            │ • Express API              │
            │ • Socket.io (Real-time)    │
            │ • Workspace Manager        │
            └────────────┬───────────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │        Auditor Microservice (Python)         │
    │----------------------------------------------│
    │ 1. Code → CPG (AST + CFG + PDG)              │
    │ 2. GNN scans graph for anomalies             │
    │ 3. Taint Analysis (Source → Sink tracking)   │
    │ 4. Semgrep + Bandit scans                    │
    │ 5. LLM generates fixes (Ollama / Groq)       │
    └────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │        AI Reasoning + Feedback Loop          │
    │----------------------------------------------│
    │ • Patch validation via AST                   │
    │ • CFG consistency check                      │
    │ • Learns from user feedback                  │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘




## 🚀 Technology Stack

* **Frontend (Port 5173):** React.js 18+, Vite, Monaco Editor, Tailwind CSS v3, Socket.io Client, Axios
* **Backend Server (Port 3001):** Node.js 18+, Express.js, Socket.io, `simple-git`, MongoDB + Mongoose, CORS, UUID
* **Security Auditor (Port 8000):** Python 3.9+, FastAPI, Tree-sitter, Semgrep, NetworkX (Graph Analysis), Groq API / Ollama

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```text
devshield/
├── client/          # React Frontend (Monaco, Tailwind, Socket.io)
├── server/          # Node.js Backend (Express, APIs, MongoDB)
├── auditor/         # Python Security Engine (GNN, Tree-sitter, Semgrep)
├── workspaces/      # ⚠️ LOCAL ONLY: User project directory (Git clones)
└── README.md


1. Clone the Repository
git clone [https://github.com/rupanjali-bharti/DevShield.git](https://github.com/rupanjali-bharti/DevShield.git)
cd DevShield/devshield

2. Setup Frontend
cd client
npm install
npm run dev
# Starts on http://localhost:5173

3. Setup Backend Server
cd ../server
npm install

# Create environment file
echo "MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/devshield" > .env
echo "PYTHON_AUDITOR_URL=http://localhost:8000" >> .env
echo "PORT=3001" >> .env

npm run dev
# Starts on http://localhost:3001

4. Setup Security Auditor
cd ../auditor

# Create and activate virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate (Windows):
venv\Scripts\activate
# Activate (macOS/Linux):
# source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install fastapi uvicorn[standard] tree-sitter tree-sitter-language-pack networkx pydantic python-dotenv semgrep groq requests

# Start the security auditor
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
# Starts on http://localhost:8000

## 🎯 Usage Guide
Clone a Repository: Enter a GitHub repository URL in the DevShield interface. The system will clone the repository to server/workspaces/{projectName} and automatically load the file tree.

Code Editing: Browse files and edit them natively in the integrated Monaco Editor with full syntax highlighting. Supports auto-save (Ctrl+S) and real-time collaborative editing.

Security Auditing: Trigger the Audit execution for file-level or project-level analysis. View real-time vulnerability detection, comprehensive reports, and AI-powered explanations.

Review & Manage Findings: Browse issues categorized by severity. Accept or reject AI-generated patch suggestions, track resolution progress, and export audit reports for compliance.

## 🔬 Security Analysis Features
Static Analysis Engine: Integrates Semgrep with 500+ security rules covering 20+ languages. Detects common patterns (SQLi, XSS) and OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities out of the box.

AST-Based Analysis: Utilizes Tree-sitter to parse 165+ languages, extract discrete code structures (functions, classes), and flag dangerous API usage based on language-specific rulesets.

Advanced Graph Analysis:

Builds a Code Property Graph (CPG) linking AST, Control Flow, and Data Flow.

Conducts Taint Analysis to track user input to sensitive sinks.

Uses NetworkX for complex graph algorithms to trace multi-step vulnerability paths.

AI-Powered Intelligence: Leverages Groq (for production) or Ollama (for local inference) to provide natural language vulnerability explanations, context-aware code fixes, and structural patch validation.

